<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rada of the Belarusian Democratic Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a> of the Belarusian Democratic Republic is the council that proclaimed Belarusian independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a> on 25 March 1918, under German occupation. It issued a series of constituent charters but could not build a lasting state, and after the return of the Bolsheviks it went into exile. It has continued abroad ever since, making it the oldest government in exile in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rada-of-the-belarusian-democratic-republic.jpg" alt="Rada of the Belarusian Democratic Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BetacommandBot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Belarus_(1918,_1991%E2%80%931995).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
